Title: ADONAI
Credit: Episode 1, "In the Beginning"
Author: The Opening (Genesis 1:1–2:7)
Draft date: 2026-10-08
Notes: Shooting script, first draft, v1. One unbroken sequence, 4:50, no words. Every shot is timed to treatment v3.1 and tagged. Timecodes are from the first frame. The animatic (production/opening/opening-animatic-v1.mp4) is cut to these exact timings.
Contact: See bible/story/arcs/01-beginnings/opening/TREATMENT.md for every source and every decision behind each shot.

[[The tagging follows ROADMAP §4: P1 the text, P2 the science or history, P5 the author, P6 Claude's suggestion, each kept or confirmed on the date given in the treatment. No dialogue tiers: nothing is spoken. "SOUND" lines describe what the soundtrack does; sound and picture are one thing (rule 2), so a shot with no sound line has no sound of its own.]]

[[Six rules apply to every shot (treatment §1): nothing is spoken and the world speaks; sound and picture are one thing; a face in a sea of change; the sea is made of what the face is; it comes down; separation and connection at every size.]]

FADE IN:

= BEAT 1. THE DEEP (0:00–0:28). Gen 1:2.

EXT./INT. THE DEEP — NO TIME

00:00. Black and white static fills the frame, edge to edge. No shape in it.

SOUND: A hiss like wind over open water. Wide. Nothing else. [[P1: 1:2, the ruach over the face of the waters. P5.]]

00:04. The static begins to flow: a current, with eddies in it, like wind over a map. The grain is unchanged. Only its motion changes.

00:06. Where it flows, something is standing out of it: a human face, centre frame, eyes closed, expressionless. Nothing draws it. The static inside the face moves differently from the static around it. If the current stopped, the face would vanish. By 00:17 it is unmistakable. [[P1: "the face of the deep," "the face of the waters." P5: your image. Build note: the filmed face as a depth map drives the flow (dossier §6). The animatic adds a faint contrast cue inside the face because compression kills the motion cue; the final render tests the motion cue alone.]]

SOUND: Before the face can be seen, the hiss finds it. In the middle of the field a part of the noise moves differently: the same hiss, shaped like breath through an open mouth and throat. A whisper with no words in it, centred where the face is. Most people will feel it before they see the face. [[P5: the face needs a sound. P6: the whisper, made of the hiss itself, confirmed 2026-10-07.]]

00:16. The picture does not change.

SOUND: The whisper draws in, and the whole hiss draws in with it. It narrows and climbs, slowly, like a breath being drawn in that doesn't stop. It keeps climbing for twelve seconds. The picture gives no warning. [[P5: the audio builds the tension; the picture is sudden. P6: the build as an in-drawn breath.]]

= BEAT 2. LIGHT (0:28–0:36). Gen 1:3–4.

00:28:00. ONE FRAME: the whole field of static is thrown onto the face like a sheet in a gale, and every contour of the face shows through it.

00:28:04 to 00:28:08 (four frames). The static is blasted away from us, into the picture: it contracts toward the head, whips around it and shuts behind it. It takes the dark with it. The face it leaves is white. [[P5: whipped behind the face in a blink, the face turned white as it goes (2026-10-05). P1: 1:3, "and there was light," the fastest fulfilment in the chapter.]]

SOUND: At the top of the climb, everything lets go at once. A hit with real weight under it: a distorted sub-bass impact, the body of the blast. Then the tail: the static itself, pitched and smeared, passing the ears front to back and shutting behind the head as the picture shows it. The release is the loudest thing in the sequence by a wide margin, twenty decibels over the hiss. Then nothing: a true silence. [[P5: "needs to be incredibly powerful," techno-weight bass with a layered, atmospheric mid-high tail (2026-10-07). P6: the breath let go at the size of the universe, built from the hiss so it obeys rule 4.]]

00:28:10 to 00:34:12. Black. Silence. The white face alone, eyes closed, where the static was. Six seconds. Nothing moves.

00:34:12. Its eyes open, and its mouth, a little. In the same frame, not after, the black around it gathers into a second face (beat 3). [[P1: 1:4, the seeing and the separating are one verse; 2 Cor 4:6, light in a face. P5: perfectly synced, on both sides (2026-10-07). P6: the eyes opening as the seeing.]]

SOUND: Out of the last resonance of the tail, one clear note, very quiet. It holds. It will not stop for four minutes. [[P6: the held note, which belongs to whatever is in focus.]]

= BEAT 3. THE SEPARATION (0:36–0:58). Gen 1:4.

00:36. Two faces, one frame. The second is far larger, black on black, seen only by its edges and creases, and it is the same face. Its brows are down and its mouth is a smile: malice. The small white face sees it: brows up, mouth open in a frown: fear. [[P5: the four-face rule (2026-10-07): the large faces smile, the small faces frown; raised brows for fear and compassion, lowered for malice and upset. No two faces share both features. Build note: the rule is the starting state; if it doesn't read on the filmed face, the face wins and the rule bends (your check, 2026-10-08).]]

00:36 to 00:47. Both climb, and nothing else moves. The large face's malice widens into glee and the glee into a wide, open-mouthed laugh: the face of something that believes it is everything, past all reason. The small face's fear becomes terror. The brows hold; the mouths open. [[P5: the faces gain intensity to the climax (2026-10-05). P1: Ps 50:21; Ps 18:26; Ps 2:4; Prov 1:26. Decided 2026-10-05: all four faces are one face; the laughing face is the small face's own, enlarged. The malice is not in God.]]

SOUND: From 00:42 the hiss comes back under the note in hard pulses, in the rhythm of laughter. No voice. The pulses grow with the laugh. [[Decided 2026-10-07: the laugh is in the hiss, and no real laugh.]]

00:47 to 00:48:12. At the height of it the dark face comes for the white one, and reaches it.

00:48:12. ONE FRAME. At the touch, everything turns over, both faces together. The ground is white. The small face is dark, brows down, mouth in a frown: upset, unsatisfied. The large face around it is white on white, brows up, mouth in a smile: compassion. It doesn't strike. It tends the small one. [[P5: both sides form in sync (2026-10-07); connection is a dark face held in light. P1: 1:4; Deut 32:39, "I wound and I heal."]]

SOUND: The pulses stop dead on the turn. The note, low.

00:48:12 to 00:58. Both settle. The upset eases into peace, and the compassion into the same peace, until the two faces wear one expression. At 00:55:12 their eyes begin to close. At 00:58 both faces are asleep. [[P5: this side decreases in intensity to peace, then sleep (2026-10-05). P1: Ps 4:8; Ps 127:2.]]

= BEAT 4. EVENING AND MORNING (0:58–1:14). Gen 1:5.

00:58. It turns back, whole frame: dark ground. The small face wakes white, already afraid; the large face is already laughing. 01:00: the blow lands and we see it; the turn: white ground, dark face, the hurt tended, both sinking toward sleep. 01:01:12: dark. 01:02:14: light. Each turn is quicker than the last and goes further: the laugh wider, the terror sharper, the peace sooner, the sleep deeper. [[P1: 1:5. P5. Safety: only the first three turns take the whole frame, never more than three a second (treatment §5, problem 1).]]

SOUND: The note climbs a fifth. Each turn ticks. Each dark phase brings the laugh's pulses back, shorter each time.

01:01 to 01:05. The change stops taking the whole frame. It spreads: the turn runs through the ground in uneven fronts, like ink in water or frost over glass, and leaves patches of every shape and size, each turning on its own beat. The patches crack into smaller ones, like mud drying. Never in lines. Never in a grid. [[P5: organic, "not like 4 screens" (2026-10-05). P6: the spreading, which keeps the flicker safe. Safety rule: the grains turn out of step so the frame's brightness holds steady; the render is checked with IRIS or PEAT before anyone watches it.]]

SOUND: The ticks multiply into a granular shimmer, each grain on its own beat.

01:03 to 01:07. The faces have turned so fast that every expression is on them at once. They blur into one grey.

01:05 to 01:14. Black and white are the size of grains and the frame is a sea of them, shimmering, never flashing. Where two grains meet there is a flash of color: the first color in the sequence. More of it every second. [[P5: the ground becomes a sea of particles. P6: color born from black and white. P2: Fechner colors.]]

SOUND: From 01:07, pitched grains inside the shimmer: the first color has the first pitches.

01:07 to 01:13. Where the faces were there is a single grey grain like all the others. We stay on it. [[P5: the face becomes one particle; everything to here is 1:1–5. P6: all four expressions in the one grey.]]

= BEAT 5. THE VAULT (1:14–1:34). Gen 1:6–8.

01:14 to 01:18. The picture has been flat until now. It opens: the grains have distance between them, near ones and far ones, and we move in among them. There is room. [[P5: the vault as the space things happen in, made of the particles and what passes between them. P6: shown as the picture gaining depth, kept.]]

01:18 to 01:34. The wildest part of the sequence. Grains appear in pairs and vanish in pairs, every flash a color. The sea is so thick with light that nothing can be seen through it for more than a moment. It folds, streams, gathers into patterns and loses them, always organic. Nothing holds still except our particle, centre frame, white, steady. It is restless: it darts and doubles back. It is alone. [[P2: pair creation and annihilation; the universe opaque. P5: the two waters as two fundamental things.]]

SOUND: Every flash is a blip whose pitch is its color and whose place is its place in the frame. Thousands of them. The note holds under all of it, an octave up. [[Rule 2, literally: the animatic's blips are the same events the picture draws.]]

= BEAT 6. LAND AND SEAS (1:34–1:52). Gen 1:9–10.

01:34 to 01:37. Two others come in from far off and meet ours. The three lock together, circling so fast they read as one body. For the first time, something in this sea holds its shape: a proton. 01:37 to 01:39: the three settle, two above and one below. It is never drawn as a face. [[P5: your "trinity"; actual matter above the elementary particles. P2: two up quarks and one down. P6: two above, one below.]]

SOUND: Two more voices lock onto the note: a fifth and an octave. They hold.

01:37 to 01:43. All through the sea the same thing happens at once. The surround is protons now. The flashes thin out. The pairs stop coming.

01:41 to 01:44. A smaller, quicker thing falls in around ours and stays, circling: an atom. Everywhere the same.

SOUND: A high ping on each orbit of the small thing, everywhere, thinning as the glare goes.

01:43 to 01:52. The glare that filled everything clears. For the first time we can see a long way. What we see is gas, even and faintly glowing, in every direction. [[P1: 1:9. P2: the first atoms, about 380,000 years in; the universe turns transparent.]]

= BEAT 7. THE EARTH BRINGS FORTH (1:52–2:02). Gen 1:11–13.

01:52 to 02:02. The gas is not quite even, and what is uneven grows. It draws together along threads. The threads branch and join like roots, like the veins of a leaf, and where they cross, knots swell like buds. Nothing is pushing it. [[P6, confirmed 2026-10-05: 1:11–13 as the gas growing into threads. P1: "let the earth sprout," the earth the subject of the verb. P2: the cosmic web.]]

SOUND: A pad of low harmonics swells under the note as the threads draw.

= BEAT 8. LIGHTS (2:02–2:22). Gen 1:14–19.

02:02 to 02:10. The buds light: first one, then all along the threads, points of fierce blue-white coming on in the dark. Some burn out and burst, a ring going out from them, and what they throw off gathers nearby and lights again. [[P1: 1:14–18. P5: this is when the stars form. P2: later stars from what earlier ones scatter.]]

SOUND: Each ignition a bright attack; each burst a low boom, at the stars' own times.

02:10 to 02:14. We fall into one of them. The glare fills the frame.

SOUND: A rising roar.

02:14 to 02:22. Inside, it is violent. Orange-white glare. The electron is torn away from ours at 02:14:12 and flung off. The sea around us is bare nuclei slamming past in every direction. At 02:16:12 ours hits another and holds. At 02:18:12 it hits a third: a flash. From that collision a photon comes off at 02:20, a white point leaving the centre, and we go with it. The glare slides away behind us. [[P2: proton-proton fusion to deuterium, then helium-3 and a gamma ray. The proton is ancient; this star is the Sun.]]

SOUND: Two impacts. The roar drops away as we leave. The note goes very high and pure: it belongs to the photon now.

= BEAT 9. THE CROSSING (2:22–2:36). Gen 1:15.

02:22 to 02:26. Black, and speed. Faint points stream past. The photon, centre frame, a white point.

SOUND: Quiet, for the first time since the release: only the one held note.

02:23:12 to 02:32. Ahead, a point of dull red. It grows. As we close on it, it cools: crust, cloud, then ocean, blue-grey from edge to edge, with bare dark land standing out of it. These are the first ordinary colors in the sequence. [[P1: 1:15, "to give light upon the earth." P2 with license: the Earth's first billion years seen in the approach.]]

SOUND: As the world fills the frame, the first real sound: a wind, faint.

02:32 to 02:33:12. Down through cloud: white, thinning to the sea's surface coming up fast.

02:33:12. Through the surface. A flash of blue.

SOUND: A muffled whoosh, and everything goes underwater.

02:33:12 to 02:36. Green-lit water, light in rays from above. A single cell grows at the centre as we close on it, round and steady. At 02:36 the light reaches it and it takes the light in. [[P2 with license: one photon from the core to a cell.]]

= BEAT 10. THE WATERS SWARM (2:36–3:08). Gen 1:20–23.

02:36 to 02:47. The cell is the face now: round, steady, centre frame. The water around it runs through days and nights in a flicker that quickens. It divides. Again. Again, faster each time. We stay with one line of descent; the others drift off behind. [[Rule 5: from here the surround changes in time more than in form.]]

SOUND: Water, low and close. Each division a soft pop.

02:47 to 02:54. Something much larger closes around our cell from the left and swallows it whole. It is not digested. It settles inside and goes on dividing in step with its host, and the two are one creature. [[P2: endosymbiosis.]]

02:54 to 02:58. These divide and hold together: clumps, a sheet, a body with a front and a back.

02:58 to 03:02. A small, soft, swimming thing with a rod down its back and, at the front, two eyes, looking at us. It is the first face since the beginning that really is one. [[P1: 1:20–21. P2: Haikouichthys, about 518 million years old.]]

03:02 to 03:05:12. A fish. Behind it something far bigger slides across the frame: armored, jawed, the length of a boat. Ours darts up and away and gets clear. [[P1: 1:21, "the great sea creatures." P2: Dunkleosteus. P6.]]

SOUND: A deep pass under everything.

03:05:12 to 03:08. It keeps to the shallows now, near the light. Seen from below, through the bright skin of the surface, small shadows flicker across the sky. They have wings. [[P1: 1:20, flying things across the face of the vault. P5: "if we can get flying animals add them." P6: seen first from underwater, so day five's flying things come before day six's land animals.]]

SOUND: Wingbeats, through water.

= BEAT 11. THE LAND (3:08–3:32). Gen 1:24–25.

03:08 to 03:16. Shallows, mud, air. Daylight, warm. Fins that push like legs. The creature hauls out of the water on the right onto a shore where nothing like it has walked, and keeps going. The air over the shallows is alive with wings, insects glinting in the sun. Plants hold their shapes. The world has almost stopped shimmering. [[P2 with license: winged insects before any backboned animal walked, low-to-medium confidence; kept for 1:20 before 1:24.]]

SOUND: Surf. Insects.

03:16 to 03:20. It is lizard-shaped now, low and quick, running among ferns.

03:20 to 03:27:12. Night. A moon. Enormous animals, columns for legs, their bodies above the frame. Birds asleep in a branch. Something with long leathery wings crosses the moon. At their feet, in short bursts, a small furred sharp-nosed creature. [[P1: 1:24–25. P2: early amniotes; shrew-like early mammals; pterosaurs and birds in the last of the dinosaurs' world.]]

SOUND: Crickets. A low hush.

03:27:12 to 03:29:12. The small creature is on the body of a great animal that has died: a huge horned head lying on its side in the ferns, the frill up. It picks beetles off it. [[P6: the body is there before the impact, so the impact doesn't have to kill it. A Triceratops, confirmed 2026-10-07.]]

03:29:12 to 03:31. The small creature's face fills the frame: whiskers, black eyes, ears up. Listening.

03:31 to 03:34:12. Low in the south a glow comes up where no dawn should be. It climbs. The creature goes still.

SOUND: A rumble, below hearing at first, climbing.

03:34:12 to 03:36. The ground heaves under it. The frame shakes.

SOUND: The quake.

03:36 to 03:40. The sky starts to fall: one streak of fire, then dozens, then the whole sky streaming down, and the air grows hot. The creature runs for a hole among the roots of a tree. We don't go with it. We stay on the dead animal's face. [[P5: the impact, close enough to frighten the animal and far enough not to incinerate everything (2026-10-05). P2: about 3,000 km from Chicxulub, the impact below the horizon; the plume, the quake within minutes, then the debris coming back down for hours. Medium confidence on the order; dossier §5.]]

SOUND: The roar, and under it, still, the note.

= BEAT 12. DUST (3:32–3:50). Gen 2:7.

03:32 to 03:35. On the dead animal's face. Time runs: it is the last time the world moves faster than we can follow. The fire stops falling.

03:35 to 03:41. The sky goes dark and stays dark. Ash settles on the face. The flesh goes. The skull shows.

SOUND: The roar fades to wind. A long hush.

03:39:12 to 03:43. The skull sinks into the ground.

03:41 to 03:46. The sky clears. The first green to come back is ferns, everywhere: the same ferns the lizard-shaped creature ran through. Then the land greens differently: flowering things, and trees. Animals pass as blurs. [[P1: 2:7, "dust from the ground"; 3:19. P2: the impact winter, and the fern spike. P6: the ferns as a callback.]]

03:46 to 03:48:12. Where the head lay, a shoot. It is a sapling, then a tree, in two seconds.

03:48 to 03:49:12. One leaf comes loose and falls into frame. It settles on the earth.

03:49:12 to 03:50. Everything is still.

SOUND: Wind, and the note. Nothing else.

= BEAT 13. FILL THE EARTH (3:50–4:26). Gen 1:26–28.

03:50 to 03:51:12. Feet. A crowd of them, running, straight over the leaf, from right to left.

SOUND: Feet. People shouting, wild, without words: the first human voices.

03:51:12 to 03:53. We pull back and go with them: a band of early humans, men and women, with spears and tools, in forest. Something is chasing them, or they are chasing something. [[P1: 1:27, "male and female he created them."]]

03:53 to 04:26. From here the band never stops moving, and neither do we. The view travels beside them; they cross the frame right to left the whole way; whatever happens to them happens on the move. North is screen left: we face east the whole way. [[P5: always walking forward, to the left (2026-10-05). P6: north as screen left, toward "Eden, in the east" (2:8).]]

The world is ordinary now: real light, real color, real sound. Only time still skips. Each time the view passes behind a tree, it is their children, then theirs. We are always on a face, the one nearest the centre, and through all the generations it is nearly the same face. [[P6, kept: Gen 5:3.]]

04:00 to 04:04. The forest thins to open woodland. They fight a big cat: it comes at them from behind, a running fight that never stops heading left, and the cat goes down behind them.

04:07 to 04:10. They fight another band coming the other way. It is ugly and fast, and they keep going.

04:12 to 04:16. Grassland. A newborn is passed along the moving line from one pair of hands to the next, leftward, and nobody stops.

04:17 to 04:20:12. A woman kneels at the edge of the path over a small grave, pushes the last of the earth over it, gets up and walks on. She looks back once. The grave slides out of the frame behind them. [[P1: 1:28. P2: early burials were rare and mostly children's: Panga ya Saidi; Taramsa Hill in the Nile valley, about 55,000 years ago. Confirmed 2026-10-07. Tension: human death before the Garden, adopted (dossier §4.1).]]

04:20 to 04:26. Dry country, and a river running north through it, high and wide and green on both banks: reeds and papyrus, trees along the water, hippos in the shallows, birds everywhere. They follow it. [[P2: the Nile, about 55,000 years ago, in a wetter spell. P5: a bit more lush. P6: how much more.]]

SOUND: The river. Birds. Feet.

= BEAT 14. REST (4:26–4:50). Gen 2:1–7.

04:26 to 04:28. They come up onto the edge of a cliff and stop. For the first time since the leaf, nobody is moving.

04:28 to 04:36. Nothing is sped up and nothing is cut. Below them the valley opens, and the river comes apart like a hand into many channels, braiding across a wide plain to the horizon. Green runs along every channel and spreads between them: reed beds, pools, open woodland. Mist lies over it in the early light. A flock lifts off the water in its thousands, turns, and settles again. Nobody has planted anything down there. The band stands and looks. Nobody speaks. [[P1: 2:1–3, rest; 2:5–6, no one to work the ground, the 'ed watering the whole face of the ground; 1:22. P2: the braided plain below the Mokattam escarpment. P5 and P6: greener than the evidence strictly requires.]]

SOUND: Wind. Their breathing. Wings. The note, which has not stopped since the first face's eyes opened.

04:36 to 04:43. We move in, slowly, on one of them. We have seen this face before, at the very start, in the static. The morning light is on it. [[Decided: the first face and this one are alike enough to recognize; this person is an ancestor of Adam. The face can be a man's or a woman's (Discussion 007).]]

04:43 to 04:48:12. The note fades under the wind. The face draws a breath in: the chin lifts a little, the mouth opens a little, and the breath goes on. [[P1: 2:7, "and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life." Decided: real time, one breath. Your reading of 2:4–7 as a recap: the cliff is where the seventh day's rest and the recap's forming meet (FR-18).]]

SOUND: One breath, drawn in, and not let out.

04:46 to 04:49. Closer: the eye, with the river in it, the channels reflected on its surface.

04:48:20 to 04:49:06. In the dark of the pupil, for an instant, the grain of the static. [[P6, kept: the first glimpse.]]

04:49:08. Black, on the held breath. [[Decided 2026-10-05: the breath is let out in the Garden's first shot, by Adam. 2:7 closes the recap; 2:8 opens the new story with "the man whom he had formed."]]

CUT TO:

INT./EXT. THE GARDEN — THE FIRST SHOT OF 2:8

[[The Garden's script begins here, with Adam letting the breath out. Not part of this document.]]
